# ts-rs fallback output — the canonical generated types live in
# gui/src/lib/generated and are written by scripts/codegen-types.sh, which sets
# TS_RS_EXPORT_DIR. Without that env var ts-rs writes here instead, which is how
# a stale duplicate appeared once. This directory is not referenced by anything.
crates/orca-core/bindings/

# Machine-specific, deliberately NOT tracked. Both were committed by accident
# once (in the catalog-URL commit, via `git add -A`) and the toolchain pin then
# broke CI:
#
#   rust-toolchain.toml pinned 1.88.0, so `dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable` in
#   the workflows installed the requested target into `stable` while cargo
#   resolved to 1.88.0 instead — where the target was absent. That produced
#   `error[E0463]: can't find crate for 'core'` on aarch64 only, because
#   x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu is the *host* target and is present in every
#   toolchain. Keep the local pin out of the repo.
#
#   .cargo/config.toml carries a linker workaround for one machine's dyld
#   (`-no_fixup_chains`, scoped to aarch64-apple-darwin only).
#
# If a build here needs them they stay on disk; CI must get its toolchain from
# the workflow, never from a committed pin.
rust-toolchain.toml
rust-toolchain
.cargo/config.toml
.cargo/config
